# Liquid Coding Patterns

## New section (checklist)

1. **Name** — Content-based: `section-<feature>.liquid` or context-based `main-<page>.liquid` (see `docs/SECTION_ARCHITECTURE_DESIGN_PRINCIPLES.md`).
2. **Liquid** — One outer root with `class`, optional `style="--…"`; add `data-section-type` / `data-section-id` only if JS registers that type. **Section shell:** for typical page bands (hero, grids, featured content), wire `section-styles` + `shopify-section-wrapper` per **Section shell** below; **skip** when the section is overlay/drawer/modal, header/footer chrome, or full-bleed / structural cases where padding-margin-background UX would fight the design (agent decides per section purpose).
3. **Schema** — Full `{% schema %}`; `name` / `label` values use `"t:sections.<ns>.…"` or `general` / `labels` keys; add strings under `locales/en.default.schema.json`. When using `section-styles`, merge the JSON settings block from the bottom of `snippets/section-styles.liquid` (padding, margin, background, border, radii) and add matching `t:` labels in schema locales.
4. **Styles** — New partial `src/styles/sections/_….scss` and `@forward` in `sections/index.scss` (or `{% stylesheet %}` if truly section-local only).
5. **Scripts** — If interactive: `registerSection` in TS, import in `theme.ts` before `bootSections()`, lazy `*.runtime.ts` in `src/scripts/sections/` when the bundle is heavy.
6. **Verify** — `npm run check` (Liquid); `npm run build` (TS/SCSS).

## New snippet (checklist)

1. **Name** — `kebab-case.liquid`; prefix by domain (`pdp-`, `header-`, `article-`, …) when it groups related partials.
2. **API** — Pass every dependency via `{% render 'snippet', var: value %}`; no reliance on outer `section.settings` unless passed in.
3. **Reuse** — Shared markup (cards, scheme wrappers, icons) belongs in snippets, not copy-pasted across sections.

## Section structure

Every section follows this template:

```liquid
{% comment %} Brief description of what this section does {% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign var_name = section.settings.setting_id | default: fallback
-%}

<section
  class="section-name"
  data-section-type="matching-ts-type"
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="--custom-prop: {{ section.settings.value }}"
>
  {%- comment -%} Markup here {%- endcomment -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:translation.key",
  "settings": [ ... ]
}
{% endschema %}
```

*With `section-styles`:* call `{%- render 'section-styles', section: section -%}` **before** the outer root and include `shopify-section-wrapper` in the root’s `class` (see **Section shell** below). The outer element may be `<div>` or `<section>` depending on semantics.

## Section shell (`snippets/section-styles.liquid`)

**Purpose:** shared merchant controls for **padding** (four sides), **margin** (top/bottom), **background**, **border** (width/style/color), and **per-corner radius**. The snippet outputs a `<style>` block that sets `--section-*` variables on `#shopify-section-{{ section.id }}`. **`src/styles/base/_section-wrapper.scss`** applies those via class **`shopify-section-wrapper`** on the section’s visible root (same element that carries color-scheme `--cs-*` inline styles when used).

**Include when:** the section reads as a normal **page section** (marketing blocks, `main-*` content bands, sliders, grids) where merchants expect spacing/background like other theme sections. Examples in repo: `section-feature-grid`, `section-home-slider`, `annotated`.

**Omit when (agent judgment):** global **chrome** (header group, footer group), **cart drawer** / **search modal** / other **overlays**, sections that are **purely structural** or **must not** receive outer padding/background (e.g. some full-bleed technical layouts). If omitted, do **not** paste the snippet’s schema block.

**Liquid pattern** (before the outer root; root includes `shopify-section-wrapper` in `class` when using shell):

```liquid
{%- render 'section-styles', section: section -%}

<div
  class="section-{{ section.id }} section-your-name … shopify-section-wrapper"
  …
>
```

**Schema:** copy the commented JSON array from `snippets/section-styles.liquid` into the section’s `"settings"` (ids must match what the snippet reads: `padding_*`, `margin_*`, `background_color`, `border_*`, `border_radius_*`, `border_color`). Localize labels via `t:` keys in `locales/en.default.schema.json`.

**SCSS:** no extra import — `.shopify-section-wrapper` is global. Section-specific SCSS should not re-declare the same shell padding unless overriding intentionally.

## Key patterns

- Use `{%- liquid ... -%}` tag for multi-line variable assignments (whitespace-trimmed)
- Use `{%- if -%}` / `{%- endif -%}` (hyphenated) to control whitespace
- CSS variables on the section root element for dynamic settings; sections using `section-styles` also get `--section-*` on `#shopify-section-{{ id }}` while `.shopify-section-wrapper` consumes them
- `data-section-type` must exactly match the `SECTION_TYPE` constant in the paired TypeScript file
- `data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"` required for editor events
- Use `data-*` attributes for JS hooks, never classes

## Image rendering

```liquid
{{ image | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag:
    loading: 'lazy',
    alt: image.alt,
    class: 'class-name',
    widths: '400,600,800,1200,1600',
    sizes: '(min-width: 62em) 25vw, 50vw'
}}
```

- First image above fold: `loading: 'eager'`; everything else: `loading: 'lazy'`
- Always provide `widths` and `sizes` for responsive images

## Schema conventions

- Use translation keys for `name` and `label` where available: `"t:general.xxx"`
- Settings types: `range`, `checkbox`, `select`, `text`, `richtext`, `image_picker`, `color`, `color_scheme`
- Group related settings with `"type": "header"`

## Snippet naming

- PDP snippets: `pdp-gallery`, `pdp-variant-picker`, `pdp-buy-row`, etc.
- Header snippets: `header-logo`, `header-site-nav`, `header-icons`
- Rendered with: `{% render 'snippet-name', param: value %}`
- Snippets are isolated scope — pass all needed variables explicitly

## Section groups

- Header: `{% sections 'header-group' %}` in layout
- Footer: `{% sections 'footer-group' %}` in layout
- Cart drawer: `{% section 'cart-drawer' %}` (always rendered in layout)

## Forms

- AJAX cart forms use `data-ajax-add-to-cart` attribute
- Product forms: `{% form 'product', product %}`

## Theme Check

- Config: `.theme-check.yml` extends `theme-check:recommended`
- Run: `npm run check`
- Known exceptions documented in `.theme-check.yml` (UnclosedHTMLElement for PDP, RemoteAsset for Google Fonts)
